<SECTION SCID = "T060004A453S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T060004A453" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "28Jan2004"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Brake Master Cylinder &amp; Reservoir</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A tandem type master cylinder is used. In addition, the master cylinder is inserted into the booster when mounted, shortening the mounting length.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The reservoir tank is integrated with the master cylinder to save space. In addition, a level warning switch is provided to detect the brake fluid level.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740026c" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.944in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T060004A219S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T060004A219" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Brake Booster</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A 10" single type brake booster is used on all models.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Tie rods are provided inside the booster to ensure rigidity during booster operation, allowing the booster body plate thickness to be reduced for weight reduction.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740027c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "5.264in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T060004A221S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T060004A221" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Front Brake</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>16" ventilated disc rotors and PE63 type calipers are used on models with the 2GR-FE engine.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740207c" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.597in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T060004A222S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T060004A222" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Rear Brake</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>All models use disc brakes with CLA11H type calipers and a rotor size of ø279mm × 10mm thickness. The calipers are a built-in type that also serves as the parking brake.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740166c" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.028in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T060004A234S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T060004A234" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Parking Brake</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The stick type center lever parking brake lever has been changed to a foot-operated parking brake pedal.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "c5930004c" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.792in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
